Usages:
  transaction_lifecycle: |
    Two lock modes gate every BatchTx transaction: LockInsideApply (acquired while executing a
    raft-committed request) and LockOutsideApply (acquired by background jobs such as
    compaction or defrag). Never mix the two across the same critical section — each is
    validated at runtime against the call stack it was invoked from. Commit() flushes the
    batched writes into a single underlying bbolt transaction and begins a fresh writable one;
    Unlock() auto-commits once the pending write count reaches the backend's configured batch
    limit, so most callers never call Commit() directly.

Annotations: |
  This cell wraps a single embedded bbolt (BoltDB) file into etcd's own transactional,
  byte-oriented key/value primitive: named buckets, batched writes, and a buffered read path
  that makes uncommitted writes immediately visible to subsequent reads. It has no awareness of
  MVCC, revisions, watch, or etcd's data model — it exposes only bucket/key/value operations
  plus lock discipline tied to etcd's raft-apply pipeline. It is a leaf: nothing documented in
  this architecture forest is a dependency of this cell, and every other storage-adjacent cell
  imports from here.

  Use `transaction_lifecycle` to decide which lock method a new caller should acquire.

---

"Backend()":
  location: backend.go
  annotations: |
    The top-level storage handle: one bbolt file's lifecycle (open, defrag, snapshot, close)
    plus a background commit loop that coalesces many logical writes into one periodic bbolt
    commit.
  methods:
    "ReadTx() -> tx:ReadTx": |
      Return the shared, lock-guarded read transaction, backed by the latest committed data
      plus any buffered-but-uncommitted writes.
    "ConcurrentReadTx() -> tx:ReadTx": |
      Return a non-blocking read transaction over a snapshotted copy of the write buffer.
      Prefer this over `ReadTx` on hot read paths that will not themselves become a writer
      during their lifetime.
    "BatchTx() -> tx:BatchTx": |
      Return the single writable transaction handle for this backend.
    "Snapshot() -> snapshot:Snapshot": |
      Commit pending writes and return a consistent, point-in-time byte stream of the entire
      store, used for full-state transfer to a lagging or newly-joined peer.
    "Hash(ignore BucketKeyPredicate) -> hash:uint32, err:error": |
      Compute a CRC32C digest over every bucket/key/value pair not excluded by `ignore`, used
      for cross-member corruption detection.
    "Defrag() -> err:error": |
      Compact the on-disk bbolt file by rewriting all live data into a fresh file and swapping
      it into place.
    "ForceCommit()": |
      Commit the current batch transaction immediately rather than waiting for the configured
      batch interval or batch-size limit to elapse.

"BatchTx()":
  location: batch_tx.go
  annotations: |
    The single writable transaction against the backing bbolt file for this `Backend`. Writes
    made through this transaction are buffered so they are immediately visible to subsequent
    reads before the underlying bbolt transaction actually commits.

    Use `transaction_lifecycle` to choose between the inside-apply and outside-apply lock
    methods below.
  methods:
    "LockInsideApply()": |
      Acquire the write lock from within the raft-apply pipeline (i.e. while executing one
      raft-committed request).
    "LockOutsideApply()": |
      Acquire the write lock from a background job outside raft apply (e.g. compaction,
      defrag).
    "Unlock()": |
      Release the write lock; auto-commits once the pending write count reaches the backend's
      configured batch limit.
    "Commit()": |
      Flush pending writes into a new bbolt transaction and begin a fresh writable one.
    "UnsafeCreateBucket(bucket Bucket)": |
      Create a named bucket. Caller must already hold the write lock.
    "UnsafePut(bucket Bucket, key []byte, value []byte)": |
      Write one key/value pair into `bucket`. Caller must already hold the write lock.
    "UnsafeDelete(bucket Bucket, key []byte)": |
      Remove one key from `bucket`. Caller must already hold the write lock.
    "UnsafeRange(bucket Bucket, key []byte, endKey []byte, limit int64) -> keys:[][]byte, vals:[][]byte": |
      Scan the half-open range from `key` up to (excluding) `endKey` in `bucket`, merging
      buffered and already-committed data, bounded by `limit` (0 means unbounded).

"ReadTx()":
  location: read_tx.go
  annotations: |
    A read-only view merging the in-memory write buffer with the last committed bbolt
    transaction.
  methods:
    "RLock()": |
      Acquire a read lock.
    "RUnlock()": |
      Release a read lock.
    "UnsafeRange(bucket Bucket, key []byte, endKey []byte, limit int64) -> keys:[][]byte, vals:[][]byte": |
      Scan the half-open range from `key` up to (excluding) `endKey` in `bucket`, merging
      buffered and committed data. Caller must already hold a read lock.

"Hooks()":
  location: hooks.go
  annotations: |
    Extension point letting a layer above this cell inject one additional write into the same
    bbolt commit, atomically with everything else already staged in that transaction.
  methods:
    "OnPreCommitUnsafe(tx BatchTx)": |
      Called immediately before a batch transaction commits. Implementations perform
      additional unsafe put/delete calls against `tx` (e.g. persisting a consistency index
      alongside the data it describes).

